{"conversation":"Ok, so strings get special equivalent if their even and odd indexed characters can be rearranged to match. Maybe I can separate each string's even and odd letters and sort those, then use that as a signature to group?","python_code":"class Solution:
    def numSpecialEquivGroups(self, words: List[str]) -> int:
        groups = set()
        for word in words:
            even_chars = sorted(word[0::2])
            odd_chars = sorted(word[1::2])
            signature = (tuple(even_chars), tuple(odd_chars))
            groups.add(signature)
        return len(groups)"}
